    "ProjectStatus": {
      "description": "Observed state. Distinct from [`DesiredState`]: the reconciler exists\nprecisely because these two disagree after a crash or a reboot.\n\n`Crashed` and `Failed` are both bad endings and deliberately not the\nsame word. `Failed` is a project that never got off the ground — the\nruntime is not installed, the port was taken, the entry file is not\nthere — and the fix is configuration. `Crashed` is a project that\nstarted cleanly, ran, and then exited on its own, where the fix is in\nthe user's code. Collapsing the two forces the interface to guess which\nhappened, and it can only guess wrong half the time.",
      "enum": [
        "CREATING",
        "STOPPED",
        "STARTING",
        "RUNNING",
        "STOPPING",
        "RESTARTING",
        "BUILDING",
        "CRASHED",
        "FAILED",
        "UNHEALTHY",
        "ARCHIVED",
        "DELETING"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
